Port of the ChromeOS "drm_master_relax" debugfs interface to vanilla 7.1.

ChromeOS hands DRM master back and forth between Chrome and frecon (the
console) on VT switches. Chrome opens the DRM device fd in the browser
process but issues SET_MASTER/DROP_MASTER from the unprivileged GPU
process, so the vanilla drm_master_check_perm() pid check rejects the
drop (and the GPU process has no CAP_SYS_ADMIN). frecon therefore logs
"Chrome did not release master", fails to take over the display, and
Ctrl-Alt-F2 lands on a black screen with no way back.

The ChromeOS kernels carry a small patch that adds a global
/sys/kernel/debug/dri/drm_master_relax debugfs bool; frecon writes 'Y'
to it at startup (see set_drm_master_relax() in frecon). When set,
SET_MASTER/DROP_MASTER are allowed for any drm_file that is or was
master, regardless of the calling task. This ports that patch:

- drm_auth.c: define drm_master_relax and accept was_master files when
  the flag is set even if the caller pid differs from the opener pid.
- drm_debugfs.c: create the debugfs bool under the dri root directory
  (0600, root-only, matching the ChromeOS kernels).
- drm_internal.h: declare the flag.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_auth.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_auth.c
@@ -229,11 +229,22 @@
  * - weston
  * - various compositors based on wlroots
  */
+/*
+ * When true, allow SET_MASTER/DROP_MASTER for a was_master drm_file even
+ * from a task other than the one that opened the device. ChromeOS frecon
+ * enables this via /sys/kernel/debug/dri/drm_master_relax so DRM master
+ * can be handed between Chrome (device fd opened in the browser process,
+ * master ioctls issued by the unprivileged GPU process) and the console
+ * on VT switches.
+ */
+bool drm_master_relax;
+
 static int
 drm_master_check_perm(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file_priv)
 {
 	if (file_priv->was_master &&
-	    rcu_access_pointer(file_priv->pid) == task_tgid(current))
+	    (drm_master_relax ||
+	     rcu_access_pointer(file_priv->pid) == task_tgid(current)))
 		return 0;
 
 	if (!capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN))
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_debugfs.c
@@ -298,6 +298,8 @@
 void drm_debugfs_init_root(void)
 {
 	drm_debugfs_root = debugfs_create_dir("dri", NULL);
+	debugfs_create_bool("drm_master_relax", 0600, drm_debugfs_root,
+			    &drm_master_relax);
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL)
 	accel_debugfs_root = debugfs_create_dir("accel", NULL);
 #endif
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_internal.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_internal.h
@@ -146,6 +146,7 @@
 				  struct drm_file *filp);
 
 /* drm_auth.c */
+extern bool drm_master_relax;
 int drm_getmagic(struct drm_device *dev, void *data,
 		 struct drm_file *file_priv);
 int drm_authmagic(struct drm_device *dev, void *data,
